WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.399 --> 00:00:04.830
Game of Thrones Season 7 Episode 2 – let’s
begin.

00:00:04.830 --> 00:00:09.549
We start with a storm on Dragonstone, which
is significant to Daenerys cause she was born

00:00:09.549 --> 00:00:14.869
during a storm on Dragonstone . After her
father King Aerys was overthrown by Robert,

00:00:14.869 --> 00:00:18.449
she and her brother Viserys fled Dragonstone
and went east.

00:00:18.449 --> 00:00:23.560
Now, some sixteen years later, she returns
to reclaim her throne.

00:00:23.560 --> 00:00:28.560
Dany questions Varys, and points out that
he served both King Aerys and King Robert

00:00:28.560 --> 00:00:34.180
– and he plotted against both of them . Varys
also backed Viserys, until he turned out to

00:00:34.180 --> 00:00:35.180
be useless.

00:00:35.180 --> 00:00:39.980
And under orders from Robert, Varys once sent
an assassin to kill Dany – though he also

00:00:39.980 --> 00:00:46.260
warned Jorah so he could protect her . Point
is – Varys betrayed all of these people.

00:00:46.260 --> 00:00:48.670
So how can Daenerys trust him?

00:00:48.670 --> 00:00:54.890
Varys says he grew up as an orphan and a slave,
and he’ll support whoever protects the people.

00:00:54.890 --> 00:00:59.891
So long as Dany is a good ruler, he’ll be
loyal, cause he “serve[s] the realm” . When

00:00:59.891 --> 00:01:05.100
he says this in the books, it’s probably
a lie – Varys has more complex motivations

00:01:05.100 --> 00:01:08.810
relating to Illyrio, and family – go watch
this video.

00:01:08.810 --> 00:01:12.460
But in the show, this seems to be the simple
truth.

00:01:12.460 --> 00:01:16.570
Varys really believes that Daenerys could
be a great ruler.

00:01:16.570 --> 00:01:22.070
But there’s still some tension here – cause
Dany threatens to burn Varys if he turns on

00:01:22.070 --> 00:01:25.980
her – which is exactly the sort of thing
the Mad King did.

00:01:25.980 --> 00:01:30.510
Will Dany protect the people, or will she
be more like her father?

00:01:30.510 --> 00:01:33.229
Dany then gets a visit from Melisandre.

00:01:33.229 --> 00:01:38.480
Like Varys, Mel was once a slave, and, like
Varys, she’s served other leaders before

00:01:38.480 --> 00:01:41.600
– she was with Stannis, then with Jon.

00:01:41.600 --> 00:01:46.130
Mel warns Dany of the Long Night, of the darkness
brought by the white walkers.

00:01:46.130 --> 00:01:51.820
And she speaks of the prince that was promised,
or Azor Ahai, a hero prophesied to save the

00:01:51.820 --> 00:01:57.330
world from this darkness . Missandei points
out that this prophecy could refer to a man

00:01:57.330 --> 00:01:58.690
or a woman.

00:01:58.690 --> 00:02:05.100
And Mel suggests it might mean both – that
Dany and Jon Snow could each have a role – fire

00:02:05.100 --> 00:02:08.229
and ice combined, to save the world from the
night.

00:02:08.229 --> 00:02:13.040
There are a lot of different ideas in the
books about how this might go down – according

00:02:13.040 --> 00:02:19.469
to one story, the original Azor Ahai sacrificed
his wife to forge a sword to beat the walkers.

00:02:19.469 --> 00:02:23.109
Will Jon have to kill Dany to save the world?

00:02:23.109 --> 00:02:27.890
Tyrion vouches for Jon – they got along
back in Season 1 . So Dany decides to try

00:02:27.890 --> 00:02:29.620
to ally with Jon.

00:02:29.620 --> 00:02:34.530
At Winterfell, Jon and Sansa and Davos talk
over Dany’s invitation.

00:02:34.530 --> 00:02:39.319
Jon does like Tyrion, and so does Sansa – she
was once married to him, remember.

00:02:39.319 --> 00:02:43.939
Davos points out that they need Dany’s dragonfire
to kill the army of the dead.

00:02:43.939 --> 00:02:48.079
And Jon learns from Sam of the dragonglass
at Dragonstone, which they need to kill the

00:02:48.079 --> 00:02:49.280
white walkers.

00:02:49.280 --> 00:02:53.299
And so Jon tells the north that he’ll meet
the dragon queen.

00:02:53.299 --> 00:02:57.480
A lot of his lords don’t like the idea – they
don’t trust Dany, they remember how her

00:02:57.480 --> 00:03:01.079
father the Mad King killed Jon’s grandfather
and uncle.

00:03:01.079 --> 00:03:06.040
But Jon says that they need Dany’s support
and that he’s the best man to go meet her.

00:03:06.040 --> 00:03:09.559
While he’s gone, Sansa will rule the north.

00:03:09.559 --> 00:03:13.709
Jon heads down to the crypt, to visit the
tomb of the man who he thinks is his father

00:03:13.709 --> 00:03:15.330
– Ned Stark.

00:03:15.330 --> 00:03:20.370
Littlefinger slithers in and does his creepy
thing, prodding at Jon’s insecurities, talkin

00:03:20.370 --> 00:03:22.730
bout how Catelyn never loved him.

00:03:22.730 --> 00:03:28.219
He mentions Cat, Ned, Tyrion, Sansa – all
people who Petyr has screwed over one way

00:03:28.219 --> 00:03:29.219
or another.

00:03:29.219 --> 00:03:34.459
By the time Littlefinger talks about how much
he loves Sansa, Jon has had enough, and chokes

00:03:34.459 --> 00:03:38.689
Petyr gainst a wall – just like Ned did
in Season 1.

00:03:38.689 --> 00:03:42.129
Why does Petyr keep on provoking Starks into
choking him?

00:03:42.129 --> 00:03:44.549
Is this, like, his thing or what?

00:03:44.549 --> 00:03:49.790
Jon warns Pete not fuck with him, and storms
off, leaving us wondering – what’s Petyr’s

00:03:49.790 --> 00:03:50.790
plan here?

00:03:50.790 --> 00:03:55.769
Some speculate that he might try to turn Sansa
against Jon by revealing the truth of Jon’s

00:03:55.769 --> 00:04:00.040
parentage – that’s he’s not the son
of Ned Stark, but is actually the son of Lyanna

00:04:00.040 --> 00:04:01.209
Stark and Rhaegar Targaryen.

00:04:01.209 --> 00:04:05.409
Should a Targaryen bastard be allowed to rule
the north?

00:04:05.409 --> 00:04:10.180
There’s no evidence that Petyr knows this
though, so he might need another strategy.

00:04:10.180 --> 00:04:16.470
For Sansa, this’ll be her first big political
test – she’s never ruled a kingdom before.

00:04:16.470 --> 00:04:19.930
Will she rise to the challenge, or be swayed
by Littlefinger?

00:04:19.930 --> 00:04:25.240
At the capital, Cersei meets with some lords
and speaks some classic political spin to

00:04:25.240 --> 00:04:29.340
make her look like a good leader and Daenerys
look like the enemy.

00:04:29.340 --> 00:04:34.800
She says Dany brings foreign Unsullied soldiers,
and rapist Dothraki, bad hombres – who will

00:04:34.800 --> 00:04:36.940
burn and pillage Westeros.

00:04:36.940 --> 00:04:41.590
Which may well be true – we’ve seen Dothraki
at war before, and it’s not pretty.

00:04:41.590 --> 00:04:45.659
Cersei reminds the lords that Dany is the
Mad King’s daughter, and that she killed

00:04:45.659 --> 00:04:49.310
and tortured people in Meereen, which again
is true.

00:04:49.310 --> 00:04:54.289
Just like a modern politician, Cersei uses
fear to win her subjects’ support.

00:04:54.289 --> 00:04:59.300
But the most important lord here is Randyll
Tarly, father of Sam and Dickon.

00:04:59.300 --> 00:05:04.440
Randyll is a powerful military leader in the
reach . He’s sworn to Olenna Tyrell, who

00:05:04.440 --> 00:05:09.009
supports Daenerys, but Jaime suggests that
if Randyll helps Cersei instead, they’ll

00:05:09.009 --> 00:05:11.040
give Randyll rule of the reach.

00:05:11.040 --> 00:05:15.430
And this has some basis in the books – the
Tyrells were originally stewards, and the

00:05:15.430 --> 00:05:18.990
only reason they now rule the reach is cause
they just sorta happened to be at the right

00:05:18.990 --> 00:05:22.759
place right time to hand Highgarden to Aegon
the Conqueror.

00:05:22.759 --> 00:05:26.720
The other houses of the reach always thought
that was kinda bullshit, and there are hints

00:05:26.720 --> 00:05:29.520
that some hope to overthrow the Tyrells.

00:05:29.520 --> 00:05:33.310
So it makes sense that Randyll might change
sides for Cersei.

00:05:33.310 --> 00:05:38.430
But as Randyll points out, Cersei faces the
same problem the reach faced with Aegon centuries

00:05:38.430 --> 00:05:43.500
ago – how do you beat three giant fire-breathing
dragons?

00:05:43.500 --> 00:05:46.490
Qyburn says he has a solution.

00:05:46.490 --> 00:05:50.870
They go to the basement where the old Targaryen
dragon skulls are kept, including the skull

00:05:50.870 --> 00:05:55.659
of Balerion, a famous massive dragon ridden
by Aegon during his conquest.

00:05:55.659 --> 00:06:02.439
Qyburn unveils a sort of ballista, which punches
a hole in the priceless historical artefact.

00:06:02.439 --> 00:06:07.009
Dragons have been killed by this kind of weapon
in Thrones before – so it definitely poses

00:06:07.009 --> 00:06:09.409
a danger to Dany’s dragons.

00:06:09.409 --> 00:06:14.219
Also it’s kinda funny seeing Cersei with
a big crossbow – since her son Joffrey also

00:06:14.219 --> 00:06:16.900
liked those kinds of weapons.

00:06:16.900 --> 00:06:21.490
This week on Embarrassing Bodies, Archmaester
Ebrose tells Jorah Mormont that he’s gonna

00:06:21.490 --> 00:06:22.490
die.

00:06:22.490 --> 00:06:26.610
The greyscale infection has spread too far,
and he’ll soon lose his mind and become

00:06:26.610 --> 00:06:32.669
a stone man – to join the others in Valyria
– unless he chooses instead to commit suicide.

00:06:32.669 --> 00:06:37.469
Sam wants to save Jorah, and points out that
Shireen Baratheon was cured of greyscale – but

00:06:37.469 --> 00:06:41.220
Ebrose says only children can survive it like
that.

00:06:41.220 --> 00:06:45.199
Some fans theorise that since dragonglass
is mentioned as a cure for greyscale in this

00:06:45.199 --> 00:06:50.650
book last episode, and Shireen lived on Dragonstone
which is built on a “mountain of dragonglass”,

00:06:50.650 --> 00:06:55.509
maybe, somehow, that’s what saved Shireen
– like in South Park when Magic Johnson

00:06:55.509 --> 00:06:58.249
survives AIDS by sleeping on cash.

00:06:58.249 --> 00:07:02.939
One way or another, Sam is determined to help
Jorah, partly because he’s the son of Jeor

00:07:02.939 --> 00:07:06.350
Mormont, who was Lord Commander to Sam in
the Night’s Watch.

00:07:06.350 --> 00:07:09.650
So that night, Sam sneaks to Jorah’s chamber
to heal him.

00:07:09.650 --> 00:07:15.280
It’s crazy how, in Book 1, Sam was so nervous
and shy and afraid that he could barely even

00:07:15.280 --> 00:07:20.720
look at a dead man . Now, he’s secretly
performing forbidden experimental surgery

00:07:20.720 --> 00:07:26.069
on a highly contagious greyscale patient – Sam’s
so much braver now.

00:07:26.069 --> 00:07:30.900
So he starts the procedure on Jorah, using
some kind of paste, which might be made of

00:07:30.900 --> 00:07:32.760
dragonglass, as suggested in this book?

00:07:32.760 --> 00:07:37.040
We don’t know the details – we only know
this process is painful, and so dangerous

00:07:37.040 --> 00:07:38.469
that it’s forbidden.

00:07:38.469 --> 00:07:42.560
In the books, a character called Victarion
has his injured arm treated in a mysterious

00:07:42.560 --> 00:07:47.719
process that gives him a magic super-powered
smoking-burnt fire-arm – and some readers

00:07:47.719 --> 00:07:52.129
hope this might happen to Jorah, though that’s
not looking super likely here.

00:07:52.129 --> 00:07:55.540
We’ll just have to wait and see the results
of this treatment.

00:07:55.540 --> 00:08:00.020
But one other cool thing in Oldtown is that
Ebrose is writing a history book, and Sam

00:08:00.020 --> 00:08:02.919
suggests it should have a poetic title.

00:08:02.919 --> 00:08:07.930
Some fans speculate that Sam is the author
of A Song of Ice and Fire, the Game of Thrones

00:08:07.930 --> 00:08:12.710
books – like, maybe the series will end
with him putting down his pen, like Frodo

00:08:12.710 --> 00:08:14.930
in Lord of the Rings.

00:08:14.930 --> 00:08:18.240
That’s assuming, though, that Sam will survive
this story.

00:08:18.240 --> 00:08:22.340
At Dragonstone, Dany plans her invasion of
Westeros.

00:08:22.340 --> 00:08:26.409
She could just fly into King’s Landing with
her dragons, roast Cersei and take the Throne

00:08:26.409 --> 00:08:29.779
– but that would be a bit too easy, wouldn’t
it?

00:08:29.779 --> 00:08:33.801
Tyrion says attacking the capital would cost
too many lives, so instead, they’ll put

00:08:33.801 --> 00:08:38.720
the city under siege with forces from Dorne
and the reach, while Grey Worm and the Unsullied

00:08:38.720 --> 00:08:40.220
take Casterly Rock.

00:08:40.220 --> 00:08:44.630
It’s questionable whether this plan makes
any sense – cause you probably could take

00:08:44.630 --> 00:08:48.420
King’s Landing without much loss of life
if you just flew to the Red Keep and didn’t

00:08:48.420 --> 00:08:49.840
start any fires.

00:08:49.840 --> 00:08:54.040
Besieging the city will starve people and
hurt the common folk, which is exactly what

00:08:54.040 --> 00:08:56.000
Tyrion hopes to avoid.

00:08:56.000 --> 00:09:00.910
The geography’s also weird – cause Dany
must have passed Dorne on her way up to Dragonstone.

00:09:00.910 --> 00:09:05.670
Now she’s sending her back down to Dorne,
then north again, to pick up soldiers?

00:09:05.670 --> 00:09:09.600
Geography has kinda gone out the window since
the show passed the books.

00:09:09.600 --> 00:09:13.540
But they’re just trying to keep things dramatic
– it would be boring if Dany just won this

00:09:13.540 --> 00:09:14.540
war instantly.

00:09:14.540 --> 00:09:17.900
You’ve got to show her fighting, and give
her a chance to lose.

00:09:17.900 --> 00:09:23.240
There’s also drama amongst Dany’s war
council cause Ellaria killed Tyrion’s niece

00:09:23.240 --> 00:09:24.240
Myrcella.

00:09:24.240 --> 00:09:28.980
And, though Tyrion doesn’t know it, Olenna
helped frame Tyrion for Joffrey’s murder

00:09:28.980 --> 00:09:31.050
– maybe that’ll be an issue later.

00:09:31.050 --> 00:09:35.650
There’s an intimate scene with Grey Worm
and Missandei, which some people felt was

00:09:35.650 --> 00:09:38.020
pointless, but there is some meaning here.

00:09:38.020 --> 00:09:40.620
Grey Worm and Missandei were both slaves.

00:09:40.620 --> 00:09:44.720
Their bodies were property, tools for violence
and obedience.

00:09:44.720 --> 00:09:49.810
But here they defy their former masters by
instead using their bodies for love.

00:09:49.810 --> 00:09:52.030
Which is kinda beautiful.

00:09:52.030 --> 00:09:56.590
We see Arya bump into Hot Pie, who was her
companion for a while til he came to this

00:09:56.590 --> 00:09:57.590
inn.

00:09:57.590 --> 00:10:03.070
While everyone else has been out fighting
and dying, Hot Pie has been baking and surviving.

00:10:03.070 --> 00:10:08.140
He asks Arya what happened to her, and she
doesn’t answer – how could she?

00:10:08.140 --> 00:10:12.710
Since they last met, Arya rode with the Hound,
murdered some people, joined a death cult,

00:10:12.710 --> 00:10:17.200
murdered more people, went blind, got stabbed,
lost her friend, slayed some Freys, and met

00:10:17.200 --> 00:10:18.340
Ed Sheeran.

00:10:18.340 --> 00:10:21.550
How could she begin to explain all of this
trauma?

00:10:21.550 --> 00:10:23.890
All of the things that she’s done?

00:10:23.890 --> 00:10:27.270
As well as providing pie, Hot Pie gives Arya
some information.

00:10:27.270 --> 00:10:31.190
He mentions that everyone knows that Cersei
blew up the Sept at King’s Landing – so

00:10:31.190 --> 00:10:35.590
it’s kinda hard to see how people are so
cool with her after she killed all these people.

00:10:35.590 --> 00:10:41.120
Hot Pie also says that the Starks have retaken
Winterfell, and that Jon is King – so Arya

00:10:41.120 --> 00:10:45.220
decides not to go kill Cersei, but instead
to reunite with her family.

00:10:45.220 --> 00:10:49.010
That human connection is more important to
her than killing.

00:10:49.010 --> 00:10:53.280
Arya was especially close to Jon growing up,
and they miss each other a lot throughout

00:10:53.280 --> 00:10:57.560
the series . There have been hints in the
books they’d reunite – but it might not

00:10:57.560 --> 00:11:03.080
happen this time, cause just as Arya’s heading
for Winterfell, Jon’s leaving for Dragonstone.

00:11:03.080 --> 00:11:08.620
But as Arya rides north, she has a different
reunion – with her direwolf, Nymeria.

00:11:08.620 --> 00:11:14.020
Arya and Nymeria were close in Season 1, but
they had to split up after Nymeria saved Arya

00:11:14.020 --> 00:11:15.430
from Joffrey.

00:11:15.430 --> 00:11:20.310
In the books, Arya stays magically connected
to Nymeria over distance, having wolf dreams

00:11:20.310 --> 00:11:23.060
where she controls Nym’s body in her sleep.

00:11:23.060 --> 00:11:28.220
Nymeria grows into a “monstrous she-wolf”,
leading a “great pack” of man-eating wolves

00:11:28.220 --> 00:11:29.950
in riverlands.

00:11:29.950 --> 00:11:34.480
Series author George Martin has hinted this
pack might be a part of the story later on.

00:11:34.480 --> 00:11:37.630
In the show, though, this scene has the tone
of a farewell.

00:11:37.630 --> 00:11:42.850
Arya asks Nym to come with her to Winterfell,
but she doesn’t, and Arya says “That’s

00:11:42.850 --> 00:11:44.450
not you”.

00:11:44.450 --> 00:11:48.740
This refers to a bit in Season 1 when Ned
tells Arya about the life she should live

00:11:48.740 --> 00:11:54.630
as a lady in a castle wearing a pretty dress
– when Arya responds “That’s not me”.

00:11:54.630 --> 00:11:59.190
Arya’s fierce and independent, she won’t
live the domestic life.

00:11:59.190 --> 00:12:00.690
And now Nymeria’s the same.

00:12:00.690 --> 00:12:06.420
She’s a wild wolf, strong and free, and
she won’t go home to be a pet again.

00:12:06.420 --> 00:12:11.950
Nymeria’s experiences have changed her – just
like Arya’s experiences have changed her.

00:12:11.950 --> 00:12:18.360
And maybe, like Nymeria, Arya will struggle
to come home, to reconnect to the people she’d

00:12:18.360 --> 00:12:19.360
known.

00:12:19.360 --> 00:12:24.190
In Dany’s fleet, the Sand Snakes argue like
psychopaths over who ‘gets to kill’ the

00:12:24.190 --> 00:12:26.210
Lannisters and the Mountain.

00:12:26.210 --> 00:12:30.770
The Snakes want revenge for their father Oberyn,
and for their aunt Elia, who were both killed

00:12:30.770 --> 00:12:33.450
by the Mountain under Lannister orders.

00:12:33.450 --> 00:12:38.950
Meanwhile Ellaria hits on Yara, making Theon
feel uncomfortable, when suddenly, Uncle Euron

00:12:38.950 --> 00:12:40.340
pays a visit.

00:12:40.340 --> 00:12:44.250
His ironborn are in their element here – attacking
at sea, by night.

00:12:44.250 --> 00:12:47.800
And Euron himself goes into beast mode, fighting
ferociously.

00:12:47.800 --> 00:12:53.490
We’ve never seen Euron fight in the books
– he tends to use words and magic to harm

00:12:53.490 --> 00:12:54.490
people.

00:12:54.490 --> 00:12:58.830
Show-Euron seems a bit like his brother Victarion,
the guy with the smoking arm, who’s known

00:12:58.830 --> 00:13:00.680
to be handy with an axe.

00:13:00.680 --> 00:13:06.060
So yeah Euron wins this battle, and kills
Obara and Nymeria – Obara’s impaled on

00:13:06.060 --> 00:13:11.980
her own spear, and Nymeria hanged from her
own whip, which symbolically is pretty appropriate.

00:13:11.980 --> 00:13:14.340
The Sand Snakes caused their own downfall.

00:13:14.340 --> 00:13:20.690
Their obsession with killing to avenge their
family led them to kill their own family – Obara

00:13:20.690 --> 00:13:23.880
kills cousin Trystane, Ellaria kills Doran.

00:13:23.880 --> 00:13:29.530
And now Obara and Nym are dead too – consumed
in their quest for vengeance.

00:13:29.530 --> 00:13:34.160
But the great drama of this battle is with
the Greyjoy family – Euron captures his

00:13:34.160 --> 00:13:37.410
niece Yara and taunts Theon to come save her.

00:13:37.410 --> 00:13:41.900
Yara has risked her life to save Theon before
– shouldn’t Theon do the same for her?

00:13:41.900 --> 00:13:46.350
The Theon of Season 1 might have done the
heroic thing – like when he saved Bran in

00:13:46.350 --> 00:13:47.350
Season 1.

00:13:47.350 --> 00:13:50.630
But the Theon of Season 1 is dead.

00:13:50.630 --> 00:13:54.520
After the trauma he suffered at Ramsay’s
hands, Theon’s changed into someone too

00:13:54.520 --> 00:14:00.300
afraid to save his sister – and so Theon
flees, leaving Yara behind.

00:14:00.300 --> 00:14:06.220
Euron, for his part, seems to feed off this
pain – he loves psychologically tormenting

00:14:06.220 --> 00:14:07.220
people.

00:14:07.220 --> 00:14:11.460
In the books, he sexually abused two of his
brothers and murdered three.

00:14:11.460 --> 00:14:14.570
He tortures, dismembers and brutalises many.

00:14:14.570 --> 00:14:19.120
He gets a girl pregnant only to rip out her
tongue out and chain her to his ship as part

00:14:19.120 --> 00:14:23.980
of a blood magic sacrifice to make himself
into some kind of god.

00:14:23.980 --> 00:14:30.400
Book-Euron is capital-E evil – and we’re
starting to see hints of this in the show.

00:14:30.400 --> 00:14:31.940
So things are kicking up a notch.

00:14:31.940 --> 00:14:36.430
Loose plot threads like the Sand Snakes and
Varys’ uncertain loyalty are getting quickly

00:14:36.430 --> 00:14:39.130
cut to make way for the central conflicts.

00:14:39.130 --> 00:14:43.700
Arya’s identity, Cersei’s power, Theon’s
pain, Dany’s conquest.

00:14:43.700 --> 00:14:49.010
And the song of ice and fire fighting white
walkers for the dawn.

00:14:49.010 --> 00:14:50.010
Thanks for watching.

00:14:50.010 --> 00:14:53.721
A lot of the ideas in this video come from
the Song of Ice and Fire fan community, so

00:14:53.721 --> 00:14:56.740
go check out the subreddits and Westeros.org.

00:14:56.740 --> 00:15:00.660
Thanks to the translators for translating
captions, and thanks to the Patrons for making

00:15:00.660 --> 00:15:05.160
this possible, including Maryam Essa, Daniel
Burkard, Zach Gordon, Klayton Anstine, Avziz

00:15:05.160 --> 00:15:06.200
Or, Nathan Garza, and Gina Penney.

00:15:06.200 --> 00:15:06.560
Cheers.

